    "refuted_by": "research/findings/raw/source_monitor_v9_generalization/stepping_history_confound.json",
    "finding": "The mechanical aggregator returned GO, but adversarial verification proves it spurious. A control window that changes ZERO weights (Hebbian OFF, inhibitory-STDP OFF, competition ON, same 5100 steps) reproduces STRICT_IMPROVED=True and floor_met=True on all three dev seeds (652/653/654), identical to the iSTDP run. The Vogels-Sprekeler inhibitory-STDP weight change is causally inert on the margin.",
    "mechanism": "Recall rival burden is 0 on every source (disjoint patterns + silent-by-construction settle), so the margin equals the expected source own firing rate and there is no rival activity for interneuron->rival plasticity to act on; iSTDP only DEPRESSES the rival inhibition and not at all for the weakest source (heard L1 gain 0.0). The apparent strict improvement is a stepping-history artifact: settle-to-quiescence does not fully reset the Izhikevich sub-threshold state, so any pre-recall stepping shifts margins, and the intact vs competition-lesion arms are sampled at different history depths.",
    "held_out_decision": "SEALED. This NO-GO does not open held_out."
  }
